  "query_preview": "..\nPeriods of weak late night scattered showers and otherwise isolated \nshowers will continue through Friday. Unstable air ahead of current \nInvest 95W, currently located over the Marshall Islands, will bring a\nslight chance of thunderstorms for the rest of the forecast period \nstarting Friday night. Shower coverage looks to become more scattered\non Independence Day as precipitable water values increase across the\nMarianas ahead of 95W. Heavy showers will become more widespread \nSunday and Monday and flooding could be a risk for areas with the \nheaviest rainfall which will depend on the track of current Tropical\nDepression 09W. Winds are expected to build gradually beginning late\nFriday night or early Saturday and could become damaging by Sunday \ndepending on the track and intensity of 95W. This situation remains \nuncertain and will continue to be monitored closely. Refer to the \nTropical Systems section below for more details on Invest 95W.",
